    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d645">

                <pb facs="0859" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">381.8121—El Mamoon, Allal Ben</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 304</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department acknowledges the receipt of
                    your despatch No. 1656 of March 30, 1922,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d645-f1"/> in
                    which, with reference to previous correspondence concerning Allal Ben El Mamoon,
                    an American protégé serving a term of three years’ imprisonment pursuant to the
                    sentence of a French court martial in Morocco on May 20, 1920, you transmit a
                    copy and translation of a note<anchor n="25" xml:id="d645-f2"/> from the French
                    Foreign Office informing you that by a decree of March 18, 1922, the President
                    of the French Republic granted to Allal Ben El Mamoon the remission of the
                    sentence which remained to be served and that the Resident General of the
                    Republic in Morocco was immediately advised of the President’s decision and
                    invited to release the prisoner.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to express to the Minister of Foreign Affairs, orally, the
                    gratification of this Government at the action of the <pb facs="0860" n="746"
                        xml:id="pg746"/> President of the French Republic and to state that this
                    Government would be pleased to be informed whether the French Government
                    contemplates offering to the American protégé any amends for his long
                    detention.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
